# Real health data — the Supabase export and any local backup of it.
# Weight and meal history is personal health data under POPIA. It is read by
# the migration script and by the trend oracle test, and it must never reach
# git: a commit is public the moment the repo is, and history is forever.
#
# **Leading slash: this matches ./data/ ONLY, not every directory named `data`.**
# Unanchored, it also swallowed `server/data/` — the entire scoped query layer,
# the one thing enforcing that a query cannot run without a verified UserScope —
# and shipped a branch whose routes imported three files that were not in it.
# Nothing failed locally, because the files were on disk the whole time; it would
# have failed on the next clean clone, or for the next person. Anchor any rule
# meant for one specific directory.
/data/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

.scratch/
